{"id": "EUVD-2026-103569", "enisaUuid": "719bb8a3-9739-3bb1-a9a1-ff99d3a0e28c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrds: ib: Clear the sg list when mapping an MR fails\n\nrds_ib_map_frmr() stores the caller's scatterlist in the MR before DMA\nmapping and registration can fail. On failure, __rds_rdma_map() unpins\nthe pages and frees the scatterlist, but rds_ib_free_frmr() can still\nreturn the MR to the pool with the stale pointer set.\n\nThis leaves the pool with a dangling scatterlist and can lead to local\nprivilege escalation. KASAN detects the resulting use-after-free when the\nMR is later torn down:\n\nBUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in __rds_ib_teardown_mr\nRead of size 8\n\nCall Trace:\n __rds_ib_teardown_mr\n rds_ib_unreg_frmr\n rds_ib_flush_mr_pool\n rds_ib_flush_mrs\n rds_free_mr\n rds_setsockopt\n\nStore the scatterlist in the MR only after DMA mapping succeeds. If DMA\nmapping fails, return directly while the MR fields remain clear; the caller\nkeeps ownership of the scatterlist and its pinned pages. If a later\nregistration step fails, unmap the scatterlist and clear the MR fields\nbefore returning.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:17:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:21:06", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1be3211e6ac77adbb1eac01314d989d243b32c59", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c42d316163f89cd23de2f3e24558177a8c29bad8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8dca3c81344532a7f05edb3d12f31f3009410a90", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/49ba5ed0129906e0362c2e4b5e21c89b2a41e115", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4468df5bcdef959fd96494e9968f323561a45f4c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e2ee0616260080376123997488b5cf8a3870b8d9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b36d32f30c3f1e58e3a5ae79d0f52836a316b36e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/58eb1b3325edac42dc6df72c80962bd53a3c8ca7"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98524", "GHSA-wq82-wxrv-wcj7"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "132df2c7-9b94-374d-97cf-c07cf3029fbd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1659185fb4d0025835eb2058a141f0746c5cab00 <c42d316163f89cd23de2f3e24558177a8c29bad8"}, {"id": "2557ccc5-15cc-3fb3-87b4-435f4c2062ae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "2921187f-ed35-3449-bf0f-efc91fba7a18", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "41f5b523-9e3b-3a55-806b-0bb273697a23", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1659185fb4d0025835eb2058a141f0746c5cab00 <58eb1b3325edac42dc6df72c80962bd53a3c8ca7"}, {"id": "448d26d8-d748-34dd-b8eb-ebbf6931fb0c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1659185fb4d0025835eb2058a141f0746c5cab00 <49ba5ed0129906e0362c2e4b5e21c89b2a41e115"}, {"id": "49221549-c185-32a7-978e-4c814704221f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "4d61dbef-b14c-32ea-8bfd-1b93bead2bd2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1659185fb4d0025835eb2058a141f0746c5cab00 <1be3211e6ac77adbb1eac01314d989d243b32c59"}, {"id": "4dc443ea-ce1e-3f90-acb8-03ac67a9c3ac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1659185fb4d0025835eb2058a141f0746c5cab00 <4468df5bcdef959fd96494e9968f323561a45f4c"}, {"id": "624c71a4-6c15-38a4-979f-9c0722ab8f06", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.6"}, {"id": "673ad351-437d-3045-8f51-45a4ee3f0b44", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "87a57573-2dcb-347b-8dc9-0d7b65e4ddff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.271"}, {"id": "8ad26d44-c8ca-31d7-b0b7-a89f290630f5", "product": {"name": "Linu